3. Interactive Debugging and Refinement

The first solution generated by an AI assistant may not always be
correct.

AI tools can:

Use outdated APIs
Generate incorrect parameters
Misunderstand library behavior
Produce syntactically valid but logically incorrect code

A better workflow is:

Generate the code.
Run the code.
Read the error message.
Copy the traceback.
Give the error back to the AI assistant.
Ask the AI to explain the problem.
Review the proposed solution.
Run and verify the corrected code.

The developer remains responsible for validating the final result.

